odb: dissolve a placed block instance into its cells, nets and route guides

dbInst::dissolve replaces a placed instance of a block master by the
cells and nets of the block it was abstracted from (its die is the
master's outline, its ports the master's pins), read from that block's
own database. The instance goes, with any blockage or obstruction tied
to it (a halo), and a module instance of the same name takes its place
in the instance's module: a new module with a port per block port, its
pins on the nets the instance's pins were on.

Each source cell is created in the new module where the source placed
it, through the instance's location and orientation (R0, MX, MY or
R180), with its source placement status and source type (a TIMING buffer
stays TIMING, so CTS leaves a dissolved clock tree as built). A source
net on ports is the parent's flat net on the first of them, with a
module net inside; any other is a new flat net named under the module
instance. Supply nets are left to the parent's global connections.
Masters are matched by name. Each source net's global route guides are
copied onto its net in the parent through the same transform, in the
source's net order, so a block dissolved after its global route keeps
its routes: the parent's router restores a net from guides instead of
routing it again.

With strip_clock_buffers, the block's own clock tree stays behind: a
TIMING instance of a named buffer master with clock nets on both sides
is not copied and its output net joins its input net, and a TIMING dummy
load on a clock net (nothing on its output, an inverter as often as a
buffer) is not copied either, so the block's registers reach the parent's clock net
through any clock gate or inverter of the block's, for the parent's CTS
to build one tree over. Nets that touched a stripped cell lose their
guides.

dbModInst::getPortCones returns the leaf instances between a module
instance's ports and the first sequential instance, that instance
included. A port whose cone exceeds a bound (a clock, a reset) is left
out and reported.

Tcl: dissolve_macro -inst -db [-strip_clock_buffers masters],
get_port_cones -modinst [-max_cone].
gtest: TestDissolve.

Revived from bazel-orfs's unmerged xs-dissolve branch (patch 0100 there,
dissolving after placement) and extended with the guides and the clock
strip for the parent as a macro (//tools/carve). Carried by bazel-orfs;
not upstreamed. Retires on a //:bump onto an OpenROAD that carries it.
