+### Dissolve Macro
+
+This command replaces a placed instance of a hardened block by the block's
+own cells and nets, read from the block's ODB file, as a module instance
+of the same name. The block's die is the instance's master outline and its
+ports are the master's pins. Each cell lands where the block placed it,
+through the instance's location and orientation (R0, MX, MY or R180), with
+the placement status the block gave it; the block's port nets become the
+nets the instance's pins were on. Supply nets are left to the parent's
+global connections. The instance's halo goes with it. Returns the module
+instance.
+
+With `-strip_clock_buffers`, the block's own clock tree is left behind: a
+cell the block's CTS or repair inserted (source type TIMING) of one of the
+named buffer masters, with clock nets on its input and output, is not
+copied, and its output net joins its input net; a dummy load (a TIMING
+cell on a clock net with nothing on its output, an inverter as often as a
+buffer) is not copied either. The block's registers then come in on the
+parent's clock net, through any clock gate or inverter the block has, for
+the parent's CTS to build one tree over. Nets that touched a stripped
+cell lose their guides.
+
+```tcl
+dissolve_macro
+    -inst inst_name
+    -db odb_file
+    [-strip_clock_buffers masters]
+```
+
+#### Options
+
+| Switch Name | Description |
+| ----- | ----- |
+| `-inst` | The placed block instance. |
+| `-db` | The block's ODB file; its top block names the instance's master. |
+| `-strip_clock_buffers` | Buffer masters whose clock tree cells are left behind. |
+
+### Get Port Cones
+
+This command returns the leaf instances of a module instance that are on a
+path between one of its ports and the first sequential instance, that
+instance included: forward from an input port through the loads, backward
+from an output port through the drivers. A port whose cone has more than
+`-max_cone` instances, such as a clock or a reset, adds none.
+
+```tcl
+get_port_cones
+    -modinst path
+    [-max_cone count]
+```
+
+#### Options
+
+| Switch Name | Description |
+| ----- | ----- |
+| `-modinst` | The module instance's hierarchical name. |
+| `-max_cone` | The largest cone a port may have; the default is `1000`. |
+
 ### Design Is Routed
 
 This command checks if the design is completely routed.
